94: ## Fixture gate
95: 
96: The gate is run before requested training. It trains the real sealed five-arm orchestrator for the first sealed-loadable fixture boundary (100 epochs), writes a real lineage checkpoint, reads it into a fresh orchestrator with the sealed loader, evaluates real head scores over the checked-in candidate pool, and sends the selected witness through `mcrl.stagec_v025.c3_panel.first_improvement`.
97: 
98: The fixture's common catalogue term is arm-independent and is the negative midpoint of the two raw model-score deltas. Thus it does not alter either model and converts a genuine numeric difference into opposite strict-selection decisions. Each selected action maps to a deterministic fixture-only bits/energy pair; this checks pooled-EE plumbing and is explicitly not EE evidence.
