225: 
226: ## D4 — Bounded joint search inside the same 30.08-second budget
227: 
228: A seed at 10, 20, or 30.08 seconds consumes that much of the same budget. Only unilateral cache entries completed by the seed time are reusable. The current joint catalogue requires a physically best alternative for every user, so completing that alternate sweep and building the catalogue is charged to joint time. Joint candidates are evaluated in batches of 32; only completed batches can change the incumbent. At 30.08 seconds no joint time remains.
229: 
230: | rule | seed time | seed gain | returned joint gain | prize vs archived | catalogues exhausted | anchors changed | end-to-end mean/median/range (s) |
231: |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
232: | `SEALED` | 10 | 311.74% | 359.55% | 54.12% | 18/20 | 18/20 | 24.70 / 24.55 / 19.14–30.08 |
233: | `SEALED` | 20 | 505.00% | 516.93% | 77.81% | 1/20 | 9/20 | 30.05 / 30.08 / 29.52–30.08 |
234: | `SEALED` | 30.08 | 593.89% | 593.89% | 89.39% | 0/20 | 0/20 | 30.08 / 30.08 / 30.08–30.08 |
235: | `MARGIN_Q` | 10 | 217.10% | 241.61% | 54.65% | 19/20 | 19/20 | 21.80 / 20.86 / 17.53–30.08 |
236: | `MARGIN_Q` | 20 | 347.33% | 353.43% | 79.93% | 10/20 | 15/20 | 29.19 / 29.94 / 27.22–30.08 |
237: | `MARGIN_Q` | 30.08 | 396.15% | 396.15% | 89.60% | 0/20 | 0/20 | 30.08 / 30.08 / 30.08–30.08 |
238: 
239: The joint search improves the pooled endpoint over its seed, but it does not rescue the free-seed premise. Under `SEALED`, the 10-second seed plus joint search reaches 54.12% of the archived unilateral prize and the 20-second seed reaches 77.81%; under `MARGIN_Q`, 54.65% and 79.93%. Giving the joint search a converged unilateral seed for free is therefore not a within-interval comparison. A seed at the deadline has zero joint budget and returns the unilateral deadline action unchanged.
