288: 
289: ## Fixed-point change caused by first-improvement
290: 
291: | rule | matching anchors | archived converged gain | first-impr. converged gain | first-impr. EE relative to archived |
292: |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
293: | `SEALED` | 0/20 | 664.36% | 726.53% | 8.13% |
294: | `MARGIN_Q` | 0/20 | 442.14% | 450.93% | 1.62% |
295: 
296: Best-improvement completes each user's whole neighbourhood and takes its best move. First-improvement commits the first strict improvement in sealed option order and skips the rest of that user's neighbourhood. Both are strict monotone coordinate searches, but their move sequences enter different local basins. Here first-improvement is not merely a scheduling optimization: it changes every fixed point and happens to improve the pooled committed endpoint under both rules. The archived endpoints remain the exact 20/20 matched control.
297: 
298: ## Reproduction
299: 
300: From `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws`:
