42: ## Scoring-panel contract
43: 
44: The top-level schema is `mcrl-v025-dual-axis-scoring-panel-v1`. Required objects are:
45: 
46: - `panel_identity`: nonempty name, information class, estimand, the exact full-buffer numerator string, energy boundary, ordered anchor/world/date/world-seed inventories, provisioning rule, and explicit fixed-point traversal order;
47: - `reference_objects.certified_fixed_point`: name, construction, information class, null budget, and the same traversal order;
48: - `reference_objects.anytime_incumbent`: name, construction, information class, budget `10.0`, and the same traversal order;
49: - `runner_instrumentation`: producer, two exact recorded/not-recorded flags, and the required-addition sentence when absent;
50: - `anchors`: identities, the three profile references (`base`, certified fixed point, anytime incumbent), ordered profiles, and optional runner-recorded per-arm instrumentation;
51: - each profile: C1 and C2 selected/reference state pairs, C3 coalition size and invariant state, and a physical outcome containing full-buffer bits, joules, and additive co-metric counts.
52: 
53: Model-input widths are checked against all five checkpoint arms. Reference profile identities must exist in each anchor catalogue. Energy must be positive; counts must be nonnegative and numerators may not exceed their denominators. The panel must attest `full_buffer_no_demand_cap: true`.
54: 
55: Production invocation:
56: 
57: ```bash
58: env OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \
59:   NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1 VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS=1 BLIS_NUM_THREADS=1 \
60:   nice -n 15 /home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python \
61:   /home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/scripts/score_stagec_checkpoints.py \
62:   --checkpoints /path/to/training-output/checkpoints \
63:   --panel /path/to/authenticated-scoring-panel.json \
64:   --output /new/write-once/output-directory
65: ```
66: 
67: The process sets a 5,000,000,000-byte address-space ceiling, launches no subprocess, pins all six named BLAS variables to one, enforces niceness 15, prints `anchor k/N`, and prints `PEAK_RSS_BYTES=...` on every exit.
